# A call by name looks the name up on each function by itself: what the program laid on one of the two is entered with that one as its receiver, and the other answers by what stands above functions.
# If the set were asked as one, what lies on `first` would be held against `second` too, or against neither.
# first.tag = tagged;  function take(h) { return h.tag(); }  take(first);  take(second);
